---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/06-04/', docs='https://formlabs.com/global/3d-printers/tech-compare/', product='https://formlabs.com/products/form-4-basic-package/', front='https://store.goengineer.com/cdn/shop/files/formlabs-form-4-3d-printer-01-bg.png?v=1761676475&width=1000', rear='https://store.goengineer.com/cdn/shop/files/formlabs-form-4-3d-printer-05-bg.png?v=1757633900&width=1000';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Formlabs Form 4 · stationary cabinet and detached clearance display" description="Inspect a closed Form 4 and read signed gaps in a physically independent teaching display." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment f4"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/06-04/">← Equipment 06-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#f4-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">06-04 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & DETACHED CLEARANCE / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Formlabs Form 4</h2><p>Orbit the closed standard Form 4. In the separate teaching display, compare a block centered, touching the right face, and slightly beyond it. The clearances are unrelated to the printer.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Closed instrument and independent display</h3><div id="f4-view" aria-label="Orbitable Form 4 with fixed orange hood, inactive screen, and an unrelated display block"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-f4-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-f4-view="rear">Rear case</button><button data-f4-view="display">Detached display</button><button id="f4-cycle">Next detached position</button></div>
<p id="f4-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. Click the teal badge to change the detached block position. No printer part moves.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached box clearance</h3><canvas id="f4-plot" width="640" height="420" aria-label="X-Z diagram of an unrelated educational box and its signed right clearance"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Fixed position<select id="f4-mode"><option value="centered">Centered</option><option value="tangent">Touches right face</option><option value="offset">Beyond right face</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="f4-inspect">Inspect signed clearances</button><button id="f4-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="f4-status" aria-live="polite">Choose a position and inspect its six signed gaps.</p><output id="f4-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="f4-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="f4-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: standard Formlabs Form 4 (<a href={product}>Basic Package</a>), not Form 4B or Form 4L. <a href={docs}>Formlabs product comparison</a> gives the nominal closed dimensions. <a href={front}>Front product image</a> and <a href={rear}>rear product image</a>, published by GoEngineer, establish the orange cover, right-aligned dark front touchscreen and black rear cover. The actual orange cover is transparent; this rendering intentionally uses a solid opaque stand-in. Local details and corner radii are photo estimates. Ports are closed marks without electrical properties.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original view of Form 4 orange cover and dark front screen with detached demonstrator"/><figcaption>Original front-quarter render compared with the product front photo; detached demo sits to the right.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original rear view of the Form 4 black rear panel and printed grille details"/><figcaption>Original rear comparison: panel, hinge housing silhouette, visible grilles and sealed marks.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Standard Form 4 envelope</td><td>398 W × 367 D × 554 H mm</td><td>Verified closed geometry. Source values are nominal; only export bookkeeping is verified at 0.01 mm tolerance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Unrelated teaching block and window</td><td>106×72×88 mm in a 128×96×120 mm outline</td><td>Centered opposite face gaps are 11, 12, 16 mm (X, Y, Z).</td></tr>
<tr><td>On and beyond one face</td><td>+11 mm offset → 0 mm right gap; +14 mm → −3 mm</td><td>Reported as touching and outside, respectively. Y and Z gaps remain constant.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register's original slicing acceptance</td><td>Slicing and actual build-boundary check</td><td>Not implemented or run. The exhibit dimensions are not the printer's build volume.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>For one axis, the centered gap is half the difference between the display window size and the block size. The signed offset adds to the negative-side gap and subtracts from the positive-side gap. This ideal axis-aligned check has no material, manufacturing or physics driver. JSON records the fixed source IDs, position, axes, units and every face gap; there is no print file, process, recipe or specimen.</p>
<p><a href={base+'form4-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'clearance-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/06-04/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.f4{max-width:76rem}.f4 .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.f4 section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.f4 .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.f4 .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.f4 label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.f4 input,.f4 select,.f4 button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.f4 button{cursor:pointer}.f4 button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.f4 .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.f4 #f4-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.f4 #f4-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.f4 #f4-plot,.f4 img{width:100%;height:auto}.f4 #f4-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.f4 #f4-status.error{color:#a54a34}.f4 .scroll{overflow:auto}.f4 table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.f4 td,.f4 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.f4 figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.f4 .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
